# L9 Claude Code environment — Environment variables template (Web · Mobile).
#
# Paste into claude.ai/code -> your environment -> Environment variables, and
# replace every REPLACE_WITH_* placeholder IN THE UI (never in chat or a repo).
# Account-level: Claude Code Mobile inherits these. New sessions only.
#
# SECURITY: env vars are stored in the environment config in plaintext, visible to
# anyone who can edit it. Use least-privilege, dedicated bot credentials, and rotate
# any token ever pasted into a chat. A committed .env in a repo is a leaked secret.

# --- GitHub (required for gh-driven skills: CI logs, reviews, pushes) --------
# A fine-grained PAT from a DEDICATED BOT USER account (not a GitHub App, not the
# Actions GITHUB_TOKEN). A user PAT's pushes fire push/PR workflows, so CI re-runs
# on the pipeline's own commits. Scopes: Contents:write, Pull requests:write,
# Workflows:write on the target repos. Add the bot to an org team so it is not an
# outside/first-time contributor.
GH_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_BOT_USER_FINE_GRAINED_PAT

# --- Governance clone location (read by the SessionStart hook) ---------------
# Where web/setup.sh clones Cursor-Governance so the hook can find it.
L9_GOVERNANCE_DIR=$HOME/.cursor-governance

# --- Shared agent memory (optional; only if using l9-shared-memory) ----------
# The bearer credential is a memory-CLIENT token (read/write, non-admin). It is a
# secret: keep it here, never in a repo or .mcp.json. Point the URL at the shared
# HTTP memory server (loopback shares within one host only — see network-policy.md).
L9_MEMORY_HTTP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8200
L9_MEMORY_CLIENT_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_MEMORY_CLIENT_BEARER_TOKEN

# --- Optional: code scanners (add only if the repo's gate uses them) ---------
# SONAR_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_ROTATED_SONAR_TOKEN
# SONAR_ORG_KEY=quantum-l9
# SONAR_PROJECT_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_REPO_SONAR_PROJECT_KEY

# --- Toolchain hygiene (safe, non-secret) ------------------------------------
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1
NPM_CONFIG_FUND=false
NPM_CONFIG_AUDIT=false
